# Front-office SEO (Inertia + Vue)

End-user pages use **Laravel + Inertia.js + Vue 3**. Document `<title>` and meta tags are set from Vue with **`Head`** from `@inertiajs/vue3` (see `@inertiaHead` in `resources/views/app.blade.php`).

## Where global SEO lives

`app/Http/Middleware/HandleInertiaRequests.php` shares **`page.props.globals`** on every Inertia response, including:

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|--------|
| `globals.seo` | Localized key/value rows from `Modules\Base\Models\Seo` (e.g. `main_title`, `website_name`, `website_desc`, `website_keywords`, `site_meta_*` if present, section-specific keys like `about_us_meta_*`, `turkish_citizenship_meta_*`, …) |
| `globals.media` | Resolved public URLs, including `meta_img` for default social preview |
| `globals.about` | Convenience slice for About Us copy + meta fields |

Use **`usePage()`** → `page.props.globals` (and `page.props.appName`) in page components. Do not duplicate site-wide strings in random components; read from globals unless the page tier below says otherwise.

---

## Page tiers (convention)

### 1) Global / “partner” hub pages

**Examples:** Home, main real-estate listings index, high-level marketing hubs that represent the **brand**, not a single entity.

**Strategy**

- **Title:** Prefer global SEO fallbacks where it matches product intent (e.g. home uses `site_meta_title` → `main_title` → `website_name`, then `Home \| appName`). For a **section** hub (e.g. listings index), keep a **clear section title** plus app name, e.g. `` `${listingSectionTitle} | ${appName}` ``.
- **Meta description & keywords:** Use **`globals.seo`** with the same fallback chain as other hub pages (`site_meta_description` → `website_desc`, `site_meta_keywords` → `website_keywords`) unless product explicitly adds section-specific SEO keys later.
- **Social:** Reuse **`globals.media.meta_img`** and standard OG/Twitter tags; **canonical** should point at the **main URL** of that hub (e.g. `route('home')`, `route('property.index')`) — typically **without** noisy query strings unless SEO explicitly requires preserving a single filtered canonical.

**Reference implementations**

- `Modules/Base/resources/assets/js/Pages/Index.vue` (home)
- `Modules/Property/resources/assets/js/Pages/index.vue` (listings hub)

### 2) Parent / main pages with optional overrides

**Examples:** About Us, Turkish citizenship landing, top-level CMS page, any “main” route that is not a single record but is **more specific** than the home/listing hub.

**Strategy**

- **Defaults:** Start from **`globals.seo`** / **`globals.about`** (or the relevant global keys for that section) so empty admin fields still behave sensibly.
- **Overrides:** When the route needs unique positioning, pass **page-specific props** from the controller (e.g. `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `meta_keywords`, or a nested `seo` object). In Vue, **prefer props over globals** when the prop is non-empty.
- **Canonical:** The **localized canonical URL** of that route (Ziggy `route(...)`), not another page’s URL.

### 3) Nested / detail pages (single entity)

**Examples:** Show property, show blog article, show news item, any **`{resource}/{id}`** style page.

**Strategy**

- **Title, description, keywords:** Must come from **the entity** (and locale), via **Inertia props** from the controller/service — e.g. translated `meta_title` / `meta_description` / `excerpt`, or model fields. Do **not** rely on site-wide `website_desc` / `website_keywords` as the primary meta for these URLs (avoid duplicate descriptions across every listing).
- **OG/Twitter:** Prefer **entity hero image / cover / gallery first image** when available; fall back to `globals.media.meta_img` only as a **last resort** so shares still look acceptable.
- **Canonical:** **`route()` for that show route** including stable identity parameters (e.g. slug or id per app convention); avoid pointing many detail URLs at one hub canonical.

---

## Implementation checklist (new or updated page)

1. Import **`Head`** from `@inertiajs/vue3` and set **`:title`** (or `<title>` child) from the tier rules above.
2. Add **`meta name="description"`** / **`keywords`** when values exist; use **`head-key="description"`** (and similar) so Inertia replaces tags on client navigation.
3. Add **`link rel="canonical"`** with **`head-key="canonical"`** when the canonical URL is known.
4. Add **Open Graph** (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:type`, `og:url`) and **Twitter** card tags aligned with the same strings/images.
5. Keep **`og:type`** appropriate (`website` vs `article` for blog/news — align with content type when you add those pages).
6. **Do not** hardcode production domain strings in Vue; use **`route()`** / server-provided absolute URLs when needed.

